# CraftAssay

Review contract: [`craftassay-review-spec-v1.1.md`](../../craftassay-review-spec-v1.1.md).
Architecture: [`docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md`](../../docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md).
If they drift on review behavior, the spec wins.

Use **CraftAssay** with that capitalization. Familiar labels:
Review, Findings, Scores, Evidence, Compare versions. You may say
what an assay is in ordinary language: a test of composition and
quality. Do not split the name into two bold words. Do not tell
the reader they can skip a word in it.

The **skill** is the product. An agent reads it and writes the report
under `<stem>.craftassay/`. npm ships the folder. There is no
command-line reviewer.

Canonical site host is craftassay.dev. craftassay.com is the same site.

Site and README speak as the product (CraftAssay / it). No corporate we.
No builder I. Oxford comma. No em dashes or semicolons in authored prose.

Do not invent scores. Use NR when evidence is missing. Do not implement
findings in the reviewed subject. Cold-eye is a different question.
